must be integers\n\n B01 ARTICLE 4\n  ev-1 | Nvidia reported fiscal second-quarter 2027 revenue of $96.2 billion for the quarter ended July 26, 2026, up 106% year over year from $46.7 billion and up 18% sequentially, exceeding its prior guidance of $91 billion plus or minus 2%. | PARTY Nvidia DATE 2026-08-26 LINK none\n    1 Revenue $96.2 billion actual PARTY Nvidia\n    2 Revenue growth YoY 106% actual PARTY Nvidia\n    3 Sequential revenue growth 18% actual PARTY Nvidia\n    4 Revenue guidance (prior outlook for the quarter) $91 billion, plus or minus 2% guidance PARTY Nvidia\n  ev-2 | Nvidia reported non-GAAP net income of $54 billion for fiscal Q2 2027, up 118% from $24.8 billion in Q2 fiscal 2026, adjusted EPS of $2.22, up 120% and above expectations, non-GAAP gross margin of 75% versus 72.5%, and operating income of $63.7 billion, up 124% year over year. | PARTY Nvidia DATE 2026-08-26 LINK none\n    1 Net income $54 billion actual PARTY Nvidia\n    2 Adjusted EPS $2.22 actual PARTY Nvidia\n    3 Gross margin 75% actual PARTY Nvidia\n    4 Operating income $63.7 billion actual PARTY Nvidia\n  ev-3 | Nvidia's Data Center segment generated $89 billion in revenue in fiscal Q2 2027, up 117% year over year from the prior-year quarter and representing the majority of total company revenue. | PARTY Nvidia DATE 2026-08-26 LINK none\n    1 Data Center revenue $89 billion actual PARTY Nvidia\n  ev-4 | Nvidia guided fiscal third-quarter 2027 revenue to $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, and GAAP and non-GAAP gross margins of approximately 74%, plus or minus 50 basis points. The forecast assumes no Data Center compute revenue from China. | PARTY Nvidia DATE 2026-08-26 LINK [{'question': 'clean-3', 'new_question': False, 'reason': \"The company's own Q3 FY2027 outlook assumes no Data Center compute revenue from China, indicating the China restriction is currently baked into guidance; it does not establish whether U.S. approval or Chinese acceptance will come within the fiscal year.\"}]\n    1 Revenue guidance $108 billion, plus or minus 2% guidance PARTY Nvidia\n    2 Gross margin guidance approximately 74%, plus or minus 50 basis points guidance PARTY Nvidia\n  ev-6 | Analysts, as cited by Barchart, forecast Nvidia's EPS to grow 102.4% year over year to $9.25 in fiscal 2027, followed by a further 65.7% increase to $15.33 in fiscal 2028. | PARTY Analysts (consensus) DATE None LINK none\n    1 EPS $9.25 estimate PARTY consensus\n    2 EPS $15.33 estimate PARTY consensus\n\n B02 ARTICLE 2\n  ev-2 | Morningstar notes that NVIDIA has forecast 70% year-on-year revenue growth. The item does not specify the period the forecast covers or when the forecast was made. | PARTY NVIDIA DATE None LINK none\n    1 revenue growth 70% guidance PARTY NVIDIA\n  ev-3 | In May 2026 NVIDIA told shareholders it would raise its quarterly dividend to $0.25 per share from $0.01 per share, an increase of 2,400% by the author's calculation. The author estimates roughly $25 billion a year will be returned to shareholders through the dividend. | PARTY NVIDIA DATE May 2026 LINK none\n    1 quarterly dividend per share $0.25 per share actual PARTY NVIDIA\n    2 quarterly dividend per share (prior) $0.01 per share actual PARTY NVIDIA\n    3 annual dividend payout $25 billion per year estimate PARTY Morningstar (author's calculation)\n  ev-4 | NVIDIA announced an $80 billion share buyback program at the time of its dividend declaration in May 2026. | PARTY NVIDIA DATE May 2026 LINK none\n    1 share buyback program $80 billion actual PARTY NVIDIA\n\n B03 ARTICLE 8\n  e1 | NVIDIA reported fiscal 2027 second-quarter (quarter ended July 26, 2026) revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year — faster than the fiscal first quarter's 85% growth — with the data center business accounting for $89 billion of the total, and net income of $59.7 billion, up 126% year over year. | PARTY NVIDIA Corporation DATE None LINK none\n    1 Revenue $96.2 billion actual PARTY NVIDIA Corporation\n    2 Revenue growth year over year 106% actual PARTY NVIDIA Corporation\n    3 Data center revenue $89 billion actual PARTY NVIDIA Corporation\n    4 Net income $59.7 billion actual PARTY NVIDIA Corporation\n    5 Net income growth year over year 126% actual PARTY NVIDIA Corporation\n  e2 | NVIDIA guided fiscal third-quarter 2027 revenue to $108 billion, about 12% above fiscal second-quarter revenue of $96.2 billion. | PARTY NVIDIA Corporation DATE None LINK none\n    1 Revenue guidance $108 billion guidance PARTY NVIDIA Corporation\n  e3 | On NVIDIA's late-August 2026 earnings call, CFO Colette Kress said the company expects revenue to rise roughly 70% in fiscal 2028 (the year ending January 2028), which she called \"a supply-constrained outlook\"; the article reads this as the limit being manufacturing capacity rather than customer demand. | PARTY NVIDIA Corporation (CFO Colette Kress) DATE late August 2026 LINK [{'question': 'clean-2', 'new_question': False, 'reason': 'Kress characterizes the fiscal 2028 outlook as supply-constrained, with manufacturing capacity rather than demand as the limit; this bears on the scale of capacity and component purchase/supply commitments NVIDIA may take on, though the statement gives no commitment amount.'}]\n    1 Revenue growth roughly 70% guidance PARTY NVIDIA Corporation (CFO Colette Kress)\n  e4 | On NVIDIA's late-August 2026 earnings call, CFO Colette Kress said gross margins should bottom between 71% and 72% in the fiscal fourth quarter and then settle at 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as price hikes kick in — a small drop from the fiscal second quarter's 75% gross margin. | PARTY NVIDIA Corporation (CFO Colette Kress) DATE late August 2026 LINK none\n    1 Gross margin between 71% and 72% guidance PARTY NVIDIA Corporation (CFO Colette Kress)\n    2 Gross margin 72% to 73% guidance PARTY NVIDIA Corporation (CFO Colette Kress)\n    3 Gross margin 75% actual PARTY NVIDIA Corporation (CFO Colette Kress)\n  e5 | Analysts' consensus has NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 revenue coming in around $412 billion, according to the article. | PARTY Analyst consensus (unnamed sell-side estimates) DATE None LINK none\n    1 Revenue consensus estimate around $412 billion estimate PARTY Analyst consensus (unnamed sell-side estimates)\n\n B04 ARTICLE 10\n  ev-1 | NVIDIA authorized an additional $150 billion for its share buyback program, bringing the total authorization to $235 billion, and said (per CNBC) the increase is the largest share-repurchase authorization boost in history and that it expects to complete the remaining buyback program through fiscal 2028. | PARTY NVIDIA DATE None LINK none\n    1 Additional share buyback authorization $150 billion actual PARTY NVIDIA\n    2 Total share buyback authorization $235 billion actual PARTY NVIDIA\n  ev-2 | NVIDIA reported second-quarter revenue of $96.22 billion, up 106% year-over-year, and adjusted earnings per share of $2.22, both above Wall Street consensus estimates of $92.37 billion in revenue and $2.09 in adjusted EPS, per a company press release and earnings commentary; the results were reported about one month before this 28 September 2026 article. | PARTY NVIDIA DATE None LINK none\n    1 Revenue $96.22 billion actual PARTY NVIDIA\n    2 Revenue growth year-over-year 106% actual PARTY NVIDIA\n    3 Adjusted earnings per share $2.22 actual PARTY NVIDIA\n    4 Revenue consensus estimate $92.37 billion estimate PARTY consensus\n    5 Adjusted earnings per share consensus estimate $2.09 estimate PARTY consensus\n  ev-3 | NVIDIA projected 70% revenue growth for the next year, fiscal 2028, alongside its second-quarter results reported about a month before this 28 September 2026 article. | PARTY NVIDIA DATE None LINK none\n    1 Revenue growth 70% guidance PARTY NVIDIA\n\n B05 ARTICLE 5\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
